  "notes": [
    "content: Fork drags keep to the dry rock and drag whatever they grab in with them, keel widows wrap what they catch and haul it under the ridge, and yoke patients still wear whatever they were carrying when they stopped answering to their names.",
    "content: Something bigger holds the middle ground — a ridge hauler, carrying more of the Carina than it should be able to stand under.",
    "content: Drag cords and keel yokes can both be picked off what you kill there."
  ],

